          "path": "_m/g/c/4/n/cork-harbour-wp/buoy-and-mooring-at-custom-hou.jpg",
          "filename": "Buoy and mooring at Custom House Quay Cork - geograph.org.uk - 1152521.jpg",
          "caption": "Buoy and mooring at Custom House Quay Cork Custom House Quay is home to the headquarters of Port of Cork and the stone bonded warehouse (in the background) was built in 1820 (by prison labour) specifically for use as a Bonded Warehouse. It is one of two such warehouses remaining in the world &amp; the only one that is still being used to fulfill its original function. \nIt has been a predominant building in Cork since that time and was the focal point of Port activities that consolidated Corks prominence as a City and international trading centre. \n\nIt is also the oldest building that is left in this City with historical links to Corks maritime past.",
          "alt": "Buoy and mooring at Custom House Quay Cork Custom House Quay is home to the headquarters of Port of Cork and the stone bonded warehouse (in the background) was built in 1820 (by prison labour) specifically for use as a Bonded Warehouse. It is one of two such warehouses remaining in the world &amp; the only one that is still being used to fulfill its original function. \nIt has been a predominant building in Cork since that time and was the focal point of Port activities that consolidated Corks prominence as a City and international trading centre. \n\nIt is also the oldest building that is left in this City with historical links to Corks maritime past.",
          "width": 427,
